  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "The Indonesian political landscape is currently undergoing a leadership transition following the resignation of Gibran Rakabuming Raka from his role as Vice President. Following his departure, Gibran held farewell meetings with staff, volunteers, and political associates before exiting the official residence. President Prabowo Subianto is now coordinating with coalition parties to establish a selection process for a successor, with reports indicating two potential candidates are under consideration. The administrative and constitutional procedures for appointing a new official are being reviewed in collaboration with the House of Representatives, specifically the third commission, to ensure a smooth transition. Various political observers and parties, including the Indonesian Democratic Party of Struggle, have publicly emphasized the importance of maintaining order and adherence to established legal frameworks during this period of government adjustment.",
